From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vkd3d-crossover <noreply@vkd3d-crossover.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:10:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] feat: add robust_buffer_access option to MSL
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem: silent memory corruption: out-of-range buffer writes landed
about 4 GB away, or 16 bytes before the view after a 32-bit wrap.

Root cause: vkd3d-proton and dxil-spirv range-check raw/structured views
and substitute a huge index when out of range, relying on the driver's
robustness to drop the access. Metal has no buffer robustness.

Fix: new option robust_buffer_access (VK_EXT_robustness2
robustBufferAccess2 semantics). Access chains into StorageBuffer/Uniform
blocks, including descriptor arrays, record a guard
uint(idx) < (size - member_offset) / array_stride using the
per-descriptor size table already used for OpArrayLength (size 0 for
null descriptors). Guarded loads return zero, stores are skipped, and
atomics (32-bit and the 64-bit emulation) return 0 and are skipped,
sharing the helper-invocation guard. Size, level and sample queries on
null textures return 0. Buffers reached through raw pointers (BDA, root
descriptors) are not covered.

Verified by: vkd3d-proton test_buffers_oob_behavior_dxbc/dxil 68 -> 0
failures, vectorized_byte_address 192 -> 0,
test_uav_robustness_oob_structure_element 5 -> 0,
test_null_descriptor_resinfo 4 -> 0 (see NOTES.md §23).

Off switch: the option defaults to off; MoltenVK enables it with
robustBufferAccess/robustBufferAccess2, MVK_ROBUST_BUFFER_ACCESS=0
disables it.
